Problem: How many ways can two items be chosen from \( n \) items?

So far, the number of ways to choose:

2 items from \( n \) (or the number of options when 2 lamps are lit out of \( p \) lamps) is denoted by \( C_{n}^{2} \). The task is to calculate \( C_{n}^{2} \) (for example, in problem 56 it has been counted that \( C_{5}^{2}=10 \)).

